]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"286b61dcc6809202f1a47e9d5d42797fc3cbef1db6fe75265a712178a5cdfbe4","event_uuid":"6bc1f6ce-7ce2-438c-8e8c-4c65fca875b6","position":{"commit_sha":"3579a8e360a7650b6368e3ccd88c1c0a698a925b","position":"1787719756309230001-6bc1f6ce-7ce2-438c-8e8c-4c65fca875b6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"57ad1b70d38cb24b65101c5861685cd4688c1be80860fc94d5e88cf4d7307e38","event_uuid":"f46d1164-6c6e-487d-b4b9-327ce90f4985","position":{"commit_sha":"7e9016122a87ccb73e4412b772d7e6c45c27383f","position":"1787721354737843001-f46d1164-6c6e-487d-b4b9-327ce90f4985"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (proven): macOS default-suite lane selects -m 'platform_compat and not external'; that marker is applied only by tests/conftest.py at collection time. The Verified gate runs _build-and-test.yml from trusted main against the raw patchset tree (reusable-workflow ref binding), so a patchset predating the auto-marker collects 0 tests -> pytest exit 5 -> job fails. Discriminating experiment: current tree collects 909 (rc0); with the conftest auto-marker neutralized, 0 collected (rc5) — isolates the auto-marker as the necessary cause, ruling out strict-markers/invocation/integration tier. Origin: caused_by 3ba8-49d5-fee5-445d (commit 920492b1), class regression. Fix: tolerate rc5 -> success on the macOS cell ONLY; ubuntu still fails on rc5. RED->GREEN behavioural test executes the real lane shell (macOS->0, ubuntu->5), seen RED first. Replication: full gate run pending post-merge (fix only takes effect after merge, same ref-binding as A).","timestamp":1787719151304938001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review overlap detector flagged 1909-c1a7-9f20-440f (brattish-ladyish-jaguar, closed) at 0.72 on shared artifact _build-and-test.yml. Reviewed: NOT a duplicate. 1909 is the same defect CLASS (definition-vs-tree skew: the Verified lane runs the workflow definition from trusted main against the patchset tree) but a different mechanism — it guarded gate steps that invoke a repo SCRIPT absent from a stale tree, and added a structural guard scoped to script-running steps. This bug is the pytest-marker-selection variant (macOS selects -m platform_compat, a marker applied only by the current-tree conftest), which 1909's script-oriented guard correctly does not cover. Independent reproduction, distinct fix site. Recording as same-class sibling, not linking duplicates (which would corrupt escape metrics).","timestamp":1787719756309230001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patchset 2 (Gerrit 2233): patchset 1 tripped tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py::test_completeness_every_gate_step_is_guarded_or_marked on all three ubuntu cells (macOS skips it — platform_compat subset). That guard (from 1909's same-class fix) scans each Verified-lane step's run body — comments included — with a (scripts|tests|docs)/....py regex and flags any repo-local gate file referenced without an -f guard. My step's shell comment spelled the literal path 'tests/conftest.py', so the guard read the step as executing conftest.py unguarded. FALSE POSITIVE: the guard models file ABSENCE on stale bases, but tests/conftest.py has existed far longer than story A — only its marker CONTENT is new, which the path-regex cannot model. Fix: reworded the comment to 'the conftest auto-marker' (dropping the tests/ path), matching the echo's existing phrasing. Surgical and non-weakening — preferred over a # predates-gate-ok marker, which would exempt the whole step from the guard. Proven RED->GREEN at the guard level: committed body -> 'runs tests/conftest.py with no -f guard', reworded body -> None. Change-Id preserved; plan-review attestation still certified (file_impact unchanged).","timestamp":1787721354737843001}],"created_at":1787719053630609001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f321930e-4e4c-4ff5-8c3c-ad013b173b4c","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"3ba8-49d5-fee5-445d"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe Gerrit Verified Gate's macOS `pytest (macos-latest, py3.13)` cell fails fast\n(~1m30s) with **pytest exit code 5 (\"no tests ran\")** for any in-flight change whose\npatchset tree **predates the `platform_compat` auto-marker** landed by story\nomphacite-desertlike-coney. All three Ubuntu cells pass; only macOS fails, blocking\n`Verified +1` for otherwise-correct changes. Reproduced on runs 32927544184,\n32927483100, 32927478228 (all testing `refs/changes/26/2226/*`, base `01ef008e`).\n\n## Proven root cause (regression)\n\nThe macOS default-suite step selects `-m \"platform_compat and not external\"` via\n`DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS`. The `platform_compat` marker is applied **only** at collection\ntime by `tests/conftest.py::pytest_collection_modifyitems` (path-fragment auto-marker).\nThe Verified gate runs `_build-and-test.yml` from **trusted main** (reusable-workflow\nref binding) against the **raw patchset tree**. A patchset whose base predates the\nauto-marker has **zero** tests carrying `platform_compat`, so the selection matches\nnothing → pytest exits 5 → the job fails.\n\nDiscriminating experiment (runtime oracle):\n\n| tree state | collected | exit |\n|---|---|---|\n| current main (auto-marker present) | 909 | 0 |\n| auto-marker neutralized (= pre-marker patchset tree) | 0 | 5 |\n\nRestoring the marker → rc 0; removing it → rc 5. This isolates the conftest\nauto-marker as the necessary cause and rules out strict-markers (which errors as\n\"unknown mark\"), the invocation, and the integration tier.\n\n## Defect origin\n\n`caused_by` story omphacite-desertlike-coney (`3ba8-49d5-fee5-445d`, commit\n`920492b1`), class **regression**. That change split the contract across two halves —\nthe workflow selection (`platform_compat`) and the conftest marker application — and\nthe trusted-main workflow half applies to patchset trees that lack the conftest half.\nBefore it, macOS ran the full suite and never spuriously exited 5. It escaped its own\ngate because A's gate run executed the pre-A full macOS suite (the reduction only takes\neffect after merge, by the same ref-binding).\n\n## Approach\n\nMake the macOS default-suite step **tolerate an empty `platform_compat` collection**:\ncapture pytest's exit code and, **only on `macos-latest`**, map rc 5 → success. This\nrestores the pre-regression behaviour (the gate does not spuriously fail on a\npre-marker tree) while keeping A's speedup for current trees. It is safe because:\n\n- Every patchset is still **fully exercised on the Ubuntu cells** (whole-suite\n  selection, which does not depend on the marker).\n- A **current-tree** marker regression is still caught on Ubuntu by\n  `test_platform_compat_suite_covers_the_core_os_sensitive_seams`.\n- On every **other** cell the selection is the whole suite, where rc 5 remains a real\n  empty-suite failure that must stay red — the tolerance is macOS-only.\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nChanges only the macOS branch's exit-code handling in `_build-and-test.yml`'s\ndefault-suite step, plus a behavioural parity guard. No matrix, runner, fixture, or\nPython-version change. Does not touch the `external`-marker lanes (non-gate, scheduled,\nrun on their own tree, path-pinned — no tree skew).\n\n## Testing\n\nNew behavioural guard `test_macos_default_suite_lane_passes_when_platform_compat_collects_nothing`\nrenders the step's GitHub expressions per cell, stubs `pytest` to exit 5, executes the\nreal lane shell, and asserts **macOS → pass (0)** while **every Ubuntu cell → fail (5)**.\nSeen RED first (macOS returns 5) on the unfixed workflow; GREEN after the fix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The macOS default-suite lane treats pytest exit 5 (no `platform_compat` tests\n      collected) as success, so a patchset whose tree predates the auto-marker gets a\n      green macOS cell.\n- [ ] The Ubuntu cells still fail on an empty collection (rc 5 remains a real failure\n      off the macOS cell).\n- [ ] A behavioural test executes the lane's real shell and asserts macOS→0 /\n      ubuntu→5, verified RED before the fix.\n- [ ] `make lint` and the full `test_ci_workflow_parity.py` suite pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"tolerate pytest rc 5 on the macOS platform_compat lane"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reason":"behavioural guard: macOS empty-collection passes, ubuntu still fails"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5ad2d09e-86a3-4d57-901d-354483089363","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","regression","platform-compat"],"ticket_id":"ad4a-f598-39f0-474d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Verified gate macOS cell fails (pytest exit 5) for patchsets predating the platform_compat auto-marker","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f87988a7-3910-4505-b625-23ecfddaeb9f","0e035b06-1481-4333-8544-7cbcd4f78531","5ad2d09e-86a3-4d57-901d-354483089363","76c5f8ff-e750-4584-953f-f88d5ee65ea5","f321930e-4e4c-4ff5-8c3c-ad013b173b4c","22f60cc9-f728-4222-b4d5-34fd0ef21f04","d59ee51f-8d99-480b-884a-7c22fa6b6507","6bc1f6ce-7ce2-438c-8e8c-4c65fca875b6","f46d1164-6c6e-487d-b4b9-327ce90f4985"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787721354737843002,"uuid":"f517566d-777d-4db5-be7e-f49d741568b5"}